==English==
{{was wotd|2019|March|20}}

===Etymology===
A reference to {{m|en|teething||the [[eruption]], through the [[gum#Noun|gums]], of the [[milk teeth]]}} and the accompanying [[discomfort]], which occur during early life.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈtiːðɪŋ ˈtɹʌb(ə)lz/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈtiðɪŋ ˈtɹʌb(ə)lz/|/ˈtɹə-/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-au-teething troubles.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|teeth|ing trou|bles|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun|head=[[teething]] [[trouble]]s}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Small [[problem]]s that are to be [[expect#Verb|expected]] with any [[new]] and [[untried]] [[product]], [[system]], or [[venture#Noun|venture]].
#: {{synonyms|en|teething issues|teething problems}}
#* {{quote-journal|title=Novel Armed Freighter Adopted by Navy|editor=T. Orchard Lisle|magazine=The Log|location=San Francisco, Calif.|publisher={{w|Miller Freeman, Inc.}}|month=October|year=1941|volume=36|issue=13|page=58|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=3Ig-AQAAIAAJ&pg=RA4-PA58|column=1|oclc=30746570|passage=No doubt the new form of drive will have its '''teething troubles''' and this may be expected; but even if each ship manages to unload one cargo where it is badly needed and then it is beached, mechanical troubles will be comparatively unimportant provided all the crew are safe.|lang=en}}
#* {{quote-book|author=R. Emerick|chapter=Mr. R. Emerick, Mr. S. Clegg, Mr. T. Warburton, on Behalf of the Amalgamated Society of Lithographic Printers|title=Royal Commission on the Press: Minutes of Oral Evidence{{nb...|[...] Present to Parliament by the Prime Minister by Command of Her Majesty}}|series=Cmnd. 1812|location=London|publisher=[[w:Office of Public Sector Information|Her Majesty’s Stationery Office]]|date=16 October 1961|year_published=September 1962|volume=II (Witnesses: Trades Unions and Associations,{{nb...|Wholesale and Retail Distribution Companies and Associations, Paper Manufacturers and Import Agents, Advertising Agents and Institute of Practitioners in Advertising}})|section=paragraph 9041|page=25|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ChY0AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA25|oclc=1015674316|passage=But we think that, for something which is so new, it is far better and easier for them to recoup if it is only a 16,000 run. If it is up in the millions it is a bigger problem, and it is far better to get your '''teething troubles''' out of the way on a smaller one.|lang=en}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Paula Lichtarowicz|chapter=The Nice New Brotherhood and Sisterhood of Ape-ish Folk|title=Creative Truths in Provincial Policing|edition=paperback|location=London|publisher=Windmill Books, {{w|Penguin Random House}}|year=2015|page=293|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=XEJEBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA293|isbn=978-0-09-959227-3|passage=They have survived four nights in the forest, and after a few '''teething troubles''' they are getting on surprisingly well.|lang=en}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Liz Vincent|chapter=14|title=Meddling Mother Madge + Dutiful Daughter Alice = Malice|location=Kibworth Beauchamp, Leicestershire|publisher=Matador|year=2015|page=135|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=YCMxBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA135|isbn=978-1-78462-076-9|passage=He was on his way to Cleveland, Ohio to visit the steelworks there, review their working practices and sort out any problems. He knew there would be some, they had recently installed a new casting system that he had helped to develop, and the plant back home had experienced some '''teething troubles'''.|lang=en}}

